> 1
1   Nu karimni natta pāun. Nu TUG natta waššiyanun.

What exactly happened to the baker's garment from the previous tablet is not
clear. The word TUG here might mean "appropriate clothing"—that is, a
disguise—or it could mean that the protagonist discarded his unclean clothing
and is now naked in the inner sanctum.

The word tawannana is unexpected here, since that is a title of the Hittite
queen specifically, not a foreign one. The scribe copying this tablet likely
misinterpreted a logogram.

